course: dictionary
lesson: 3252
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «Epiphany» is one of them. Read the sentence first, then ask: is this about a feast, a sudden understanding, or something appearing?
explain: «Epiphany, on 6 January, remembers the wise men's visit and Jesus being shown to the whole world.» The date and the wise men are the clues. Here Epiphany is a Christian feast.
explain: Now look at «have an epiphany» in a story. A character who has an epiphany suddenly sees the truth about something. There is no date or feast here, so the clues point to a sudden moment of understanding.
fact: Epiphany is a noun. When it names the feast, it has a capital E: the Epiphany.
fact: The Epiphany falls on 6 January, twelve days after Christmas.
fact: The Epiphany remembers the wise men, also called the Magi, visiting the baby Jesus.
fact: «An epiphany» can mean a sudden moment when you understand something important.
fact: In some countries children get presents on the Epiphany, and in France families share la galette des rois.
exercise: «Epiphany, on 6 January, remembers the wise men's visit.» Which feast is this? | Diwali | *The Epiphany | Halloween | Easter
exercise: In a story, «Mia had an epiphany while she was doing her sums.» What does epiphany mean here? | *A sudden moment of understanding | A long, slow walk | A trip to the seaside | A type of cake
exercise: On which day is the Epiphany? | 1 January | 25 December | 31 October | *6 January
test: «It begins with Advent, four weeks of getting ready, then Christmas for Jesus' birth and Epiphany for the wise men who came from far away.» Who visited the baby Jesus at Epiphany? | *The wise men | The king's soldiers | The children of the town | The shepherds
test: What does «a sudden epiphany» tell you about how it happens? | It happens slowly over many years | It happens in a forgotten dream | *It happens all at once | It happens only at Christmas
exam: In «the feast of the Epiphany», what does epiphany mean? | A bright, glowing light | *A Christian feast remembering the wise men | A sudden appearance of a ghost | A cold winter walk
